    "thumbnailUrl": "https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/-0aDEE3r1-4/hqdefault.jpg",
    "transcript": "How do I get a stretch under the shoulder blade? Yes, this question has come up several times in reception work, and let's answer it thoroughly now. Typically the symptoms have started without any single injury, but repetitive strain may be causing the whole problem - whether it's work- or leisure-related strain. Symptoms sometimes may feel unilateral, on the right or on the left, under the shoulder blade, between the shoulder blades, or above the shoulder blade. If your typical symptoms intensify during inhalation or exhalation, then it's very likely that the intercostal muscles are causing these symptoms.\n---",
